<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samuel Sharpe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801–1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samuel Sharpe was an enslaved Baptist deacon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> who planned and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baptist-war">Christmas Rebellion</a> of 1831–1832, known as the Baptist War. He intended a peaceful general strike for wages, which turned into a widespread armed revolt across western Jamaica. He was hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montego-bay">Montego Bay</a> in May 1832 and is honoured as a National Hero of Jamaica.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-sharpe.jpg" alt="Samuel Sharpe" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: english wikipedia user Pozole · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samsharpe.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
